senses.gloss:
1 Eating, taking food,
eating, drinking &c.
--2 Food;
जंभशब्दोऽभ्यवहारार्थवाची Kāśi.;
˚संवादापेक्षी M. 4; V. 2; Ratn. 2.

अभ्यश् {c5c} A. (P. also in Ved.)
 To pervade, reach to, get, gain;
to make oneself master of.

अभ्यस् {c4c} P.
1 To practise,
exercise; धन्यो वन्यमतंगजः
परिचयप्रागल्भ्यमभ्यस्यति Māl. 9. 32;
अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारं R. 13. 67;
Ms. 11. 107.
--2 To repeat, perform
repeatedly; मृगकुलं रोमंथमभ्यस्यतु Ś. 2. 6;
अभ्यस्यंति तटाघातं Ku. 2. 50;
K. 183.
--3 To learn, study, acquire
or learn by practice, recite, read;
वेदमेव सदाभ्यस्येत् Ms. 2. 166;
4. 147; 4. 149; Y. 3. 204; K. 79.
--4
To throw down upon, heap one
upon another, accumulate, lay on (Ved.).
--5 To throw or fling at, shoot or
aim at (as arrows).

अभ्यसूयक a. (यिका f.) Jealous,
envious; a detractor, calumniator;
मामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषंतोऽभ्यसूयकाः Bg. 16. 18.

अभ्याधा {c3c} U. To lay on, add
(fuel &c.) to apply, throw under;
Ms. 8. 372; यथाग्निरभ्याहितं दहति Śat. Br.

अभ्याहित p. p. Laid down, put on;
˚पशुः a sort of gift or present;
P. VI. 3. 10 Sk.

अभ्युत्था {c1c} P. To rise for another,
rise in honour of, rise to greet;
नाभ्युत्तिष्ठंति गुरून् K. 108; Ś. 3;
M. 5. 6; Śi. 4. 68.
